# Family Beacon local development settings.
#
# Copy to `.env` (scripts/setup.sh does this for you). The helper scripts in
# scripts/ load it; nothing here is required. There are no cloud credentials
# or server URLs, by design: the app has no backend.
#
# App behavior (transport mode, mock exchange interval, log level) is set in
# apps/mobile/src/config.ts and can be changed at runtime from
# Settings > Developer. It is not read from this file, which avoids needing a
# native config module.

# Rust log filter for `pnpm simulate` and tests that install a logger.
RUST_LOG=beacon_sync_core=debug

# Metro bundler port, if 8081 is already taken. Also pass --port to
# `pnpm start` and `pnpm android` / `pnpm ios` when you change it.
RCT_METRO_PORT=8081

# Android SDK location, if not already exported by your shell profile.
# ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Library/Android/sdk

# iOS: build with dynamically linked frameworks (rarely needed).
# USE_FRAMEWORKS=dynamic
